# The ssh case's server: the host's OpenSSH sshd, run as the user who
# runs the tests (serve), on the loopback, which the board reaches at
# 10.0.2.2. It knows only the case's user key and the case's host key,
# and every login runs the case's remote script, not the user's shell,
# so the user's own shell and its rc files are out of it. @DIR@ is the
# case's directory and @RUN@ where serve put the host key, as sshd wants
# it, readable only by the user.
ListenAddress 127.0.0.1
HostKey @RUN@/host_key
PidFile none
UsePAM no
StrictModes no
AuthorizedKeysFile @DIR@/authorized_keys
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
ForceCommand @DIR@/remote
PrintMotd no
LogLevel INFO
